#: ../../maths/american.md:1 bef2982ca7b4480fbc374a7a94c60660
msgid "Early exercise: American and Bermudan"
msgstr "提前履約：美式與百慕達式"

#: ../../maths/american.md:3 8dfb233804ae4f6ca40c45570b9c0ba9
msgid ""
"An American option can be exercised at any time up to expiry, so its "
"value is not the solution of the Black-Scholes equation but of a *free "
"boundary* problem:"
msgstr "美式選擇權在到期前的任何時點都可以履約，因此它的價值不是 Black-Scholes 方程式的解，而是一個*自由邊界*問題的解："

#: ../../maths/american.md:7 fcedeb6639044bcc8052da4f5cc4825b
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"V(S,t) = \\max\\Big(\\text{payoff}(S),\\ \\mathbb{E}\\big[e^{-r\\,dt} "
"V(S_{t+dt}, t+dt)\\big]\\Big),"
msgstr ""

#: ../../maths/american.md:9 9f279e4512dd4fe6ae792f5ef1b3c15c
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"with the continuation value satisfying the Black-Scholes equation "
"wherever early exercise is not optimal. The boundary between the two "
"regions — the critical price $S^{\\ast}(t)$ — is part of the answer, "
"which is what makes the problem hard and why this build offers four "
"routes to it."
msgstr "其中在提前履約並非最適的區域，續持價值滿足 Black-Scholes 方程式。兩個區域之間的邊界——臨界價格 $S^{\\ast}(t)$——本身就是答案的一部分，這正是這個問題困難的原因，也是這個版本為它提供四條路徑的原因。"

#: ../../maths/american.md:14 70df0b21899047debf03100cd9897ec1
msgid ""
"A **Bermudan** option is the same recursion with the maximum taken only "
"on the exercise dates. It is a lattice or grid problem by nature; there "
"is no closed form."
msgstr "**百慕達式**選擇權是同一組遞迴，只是取極大值的動作只在各履約日進行。它本質上是格點或網格問題；沒有封閉解。"

#: ../../maths/american.md:19 dd38a48d93f441cb9686116e8dd4b922
msgid ""
"For a call on a non-dividend-paying asset ($q = 0$) early exercise is "
"never optimal and the American price equals the European one. If your "
"American call prices identically to the European, check the dividend "
"curve before assuming a bug."
msgstr "對不配息資產（$q = 0$）的買權而言，提前履約永遠不是最適的，美式價格等於歐式價格。如果你的美式買權和歐式算出完全一樣的價格，先檢查股利曲線，再懷疑有 bug。"

#: ../../maths/american.md:25 f96d4b07bc6d41b3b7296d5b5e9e912d
msgid "The three approximations"
msgstr "三種近似法"

#: ../../maths/american.md:27 7b9a902c82084eebbc350547a7d35413
msgid ""
"QuantLib has three closed-form approximations and they **disagree in the "
"third decimal**, so this service refuses to pick one for you. Each "
"assumes a different simplification of the exercise boundary."
msgstr "QuantLib 有三種封閉解近似法，而它們**在小數第三位就不一致**，所以本服務拒絕替你挑一個。每一種對履約邊界所做的簡化都不同。"

#: ../../maths/american.md:31 71b08a2854514c1a8c0c423e6972c2ca
msgid ""
"**Barone-Adesi-Whaley (1987).** Writes the American value as the European"
" value plus an early-exercise premium, and drops a term that is small "
"when the discount factor is close to one:"
msgstr "**Barone-Adesi-Whaley**（1987）。把美式價值寫成歐式價值加上一項提前履約溢價，並捨去一個在折現因子接近一時很小的項："

#: ../../maths/american.md:35 9a19736ddd104516864122f7dec3b195
msgid ""
"V_{\\text{Am}} = V_{\\text{Eu}} + "
"A_2\\left(\\frac{S}{S^{\\ast}}\\right)^{q_2},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"q_2 = \\frac{-(N-1) + \\sqrt{(N-1)^2 + 4M/k}}{2},"
msgstr ""

#: ../../maths/american.md:39 910a67de0e964738853c55dfbd6af240
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"with $M = 2r/\\sigma^2$, $N = 2b/\\sigma^2$ and $k = 1 - e^{-rT}$. The "
"critical price $S^{\\ast}$ is found by a one-dimensional iteration. Fast,"
" and least accurate for long maturities where $k$ is far from small."
msgstr "其中 $M = 2r/\\sigma^2$、$N = 2b/\\sigma^2$、$k = 1 - e^{-rT}$。臨界價格 $S^{\\ast}$ 以一維迭代求得。快，但在 $k$ 離小很遠的長天期上最不準。"

#: ../../maths/american.md:43 02e9fc396e1448feb191eeb022eb2316
msgid ""
"**Bjerksund-Stensland (1993/2002).** Approximates the exercise boundary "
"by a *flat* trigger $X$ and prices the resulting barrier-like claim in "
"closed form, with"
msgstr "**Bjerksund-Stensland**（1993/2002）。以一個*平坦*的觸發水準 $X$ 近似履約邊界，再以封閉解為由此得到的類障礙請求權計價，其中"

#: ../../maths/american.md:47 86f5beff52134473aced9cd0000d14cf
msgid ""
"\\beta = \\left(\\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{b}{\\sigma^2}\\right)\n"
"        + \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{b}{\\sigma^2} - \\frac{1}{2}\\right)^2 + "
"\\frac{2r}{\\sigma^2}}."
msgstr ""

#: ../../maths/american.md:50 a4f08c4bba2b4768b10509e702b53aba
msgid ""
"Generally the better of the two originals, and the usual default "
"elsewhere in the industry."
msgstr "一般而言是兩個原始方法中較好的一個，也是業界其他地方常見的預設值。"

#: ../../maths/american.md:53 eca9a5b372154c3388e7c4a96433ba9f
msgid ""
"**Ju-Zhong (1999).** A correction to the quadratic method that restores "
"the term Barone-Adesi-Whaley drops, at the cost of one more evaluation. "
"Usually closest to a fine lattice, which is the practical test."
msgstr "**Ju-Zhong**（1999）。對二次法的修正，把 Barone-Adesi-Whaley 捨去的那一項補回來，代價是多算一次。通常最接近細格點的結果，而那正是實務上的判準。"

#: ../../maths/american.md:57 2575a592f44a4536a554cffce551cb45
msgid ""
"If a number has to be defensible rather than fast, price the same trade "
"on a lattice with several thousand steps and use that as the reference."
msgstr "如果要的是一個站得住腳而不是快的數字，就用幾千步的格點為同一筆交易計價，並以它為基準。"

#: ../../maths/american.md:60 4c49c367de524046b87f0e90d3301e49
msgid "Binomial trees"
msgstr "二元樹"

#: ../../maths/american.md:62 a3569a65d749433a835a0b03824a4de9
msgid ""
"A lattice discretises the log-price $x = \\ln S$ into steps of $\\Delta t"
" = T/n$ and solves the recursion backwards from the payoff, taking the "
"maximum against intrinsic value at every node (or at the Bermudan dates "
"only):"
msgstr "格點把對數價格 $x = \\ln S$ 離散成 $\\Delta t = T/n$ 的步伐，並從收益函數由後往前解遞迴，在每個節點（或僅在百慕達式的各履約日）與內含價值取極大："

#: ../../maths/american.md:66 e630ccc8ea264fb1aa12dcca366e4033
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"V_{i,j} = \\max\\Big(\\text{payoff}(S_{i,j}),\\ e^{-r\\Delta t}\\big(p_u "
"V_{i+1,j+1} + p_d V_{i+1,j-1}\\big)\\Big)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../maths/american.md:68 840d7698822e4dd8974ea1621715d7b5
msgid "All seven trees are built on the **log process** with per-step drift"
msgstr "七種樹全都建立在**對數過程**上，每一步的漂移為"

#: ../../maths/american.md:70 879700df31484e3eb0310eb67f3a91a6
#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\nu\\,\\Delta t = \\left(r - q - \\tfrac{1}{2}\\sigma^2\\right)\\Delta t,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../maths/american.md:72 dbaa79604759443ea8fa0cc0145dccfe
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"which is why the probabilities below carry $\\nu$ rather than "
"$e^{(r-q)\\Delta t}$. These are QuantLib's own parameterisations, from "
"`ql/methods/lattices/binomialtree.cpp`:"
msgstr "這也是為什麼下面的機率帶的是 $\\nu$ 而不是 $e^{(r-q)\\Delta t}$。以下是 QuantLib 自己的參數化，出自 `ql/methods/lattices/binomialtree.cpp`："

#: ../../maths/american.md:18 1057989db1554648857d350eecb004f1
msgid "Tree"
msgstr "樹"

#: ../../maths/american.md:18 7f9e955d7c1e4b009d80e27d35aa8825
msgid "Jump"
msgstr "跳幅"

#: ../../maths/american.md:18 b3815c27e7bd492b8dbecc8e76692248
msgid "Probability"
msgstr "機率"

#: ../../maths/american.md:18 39e427c49b904453a594ec604e34c815
msgid "Cox-Ross-Rubinstein"
msgstr "Cox-Ross-Rubinstein"

#: ../../maths/american.md:18 8a884e32c5ed42d2abefdb84d6fe2515
#, python-brace-format
msgid "$\\Delta x = \\sigma\\sqrt{\\Delta t}$"
msgstr ""

#: ../../maths/american.md:18 f5b8b7328c044647bd8bd8c19308a22e
#, python-brace-format
msgid "$p_u = \\tfrac{1}{2} + \\tfrac{1}{2}\\dfrac{\\nu \\Delta t}{\\Delta x}$"
msgstr ""

#: ../../maths/american.md:18 37c70faf581c44ebbc7ec7fefc2309fe
msgid "Jarrow-Rudd"
msgstr "Jarrow-Rudd"

#: ../../maths/american.md:18 6a885397269940dc81f83f9b5e0e65e6
#, python-brace-format
msgid "$\\Delta x = \\sigma\\sqrt{\\Delta t}$, nodes drift by $\\nu\\Delta t$"
msgstr ""

#: ../../maths/american.md:18 ac046766f6f84cc69168b8dfec23f809
#: e0fcf2df1cd1416ab7a182387f5f361b
#, python-brace-format
msgid "$p_u = \\tfrac{1}{2}$"
msgstr ""

#: ../../maths/american.md:18 ebb0cfa98b4646bcb78c2add56fbbd8d
msgid "Additive equiprobabilities"
msgstr "加法等機率"

#: ../../maths/american.md:18 13a93fee9eeb436aa04063488bfb8e9a
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"$\\Delta x = -\\tfrac{1}{2}\\nu\\Delta t + "
"\\tfrac{1}{2}\\sqrt{4\\sigma^2\\Delta t - 3\\nu^2\\Delta t^2}$"
msgstr ""

#: ../../maths/american.md:18 4c1456526d1b4434b194ae8d1591834c
msgid "Trigeorgis"
msgstr "Trigeorgis"

#: ../../maths/american.md:18 14211963e67645a3a2e9146d6b8c887d
#, python-brace-format
msgid "$\\Delta x = \\sqrt{\\sigma^2\\Delta t + \\nu^2\\Delta t^2}$"
msgstr ""

#: ../../maths/american.md:18 3d15f5a2c53b492b9cc342d5e8c283bd
#, python-brace-format
msgid "$p_u = \\tfrac{1}{2} + \\tfrac{1}{2}\\dfrac{\\nu\\Delta t}{\\Delta x}$"
msgstr ""

#: ../../maths/american.md:18 9669d85ed1f2437fb03112bb468f3c1a
msgid "Tian"
msgstr "Tian"

#: ../../maths/american.md:18 f97c415e5ff94516ab940e8e017b896e
#, python-brace-format
msgid "moment-matched $u, d$ from $q = e^{\\sigma^2\\Delta t}$"
msgstr "由 $q = e^{\\sigma^2\\Delta t}$ 動差匹配出的 $u, d$"

#: ../../maths/american.md:18 61abb4181215431d81752bee9fdefab7
#, python-brace-format
msgid "$p_u = \\dfrac{\\tilde r - d}{u - d}$"
msgstr ""

#: ../../maths/american.md:18 0ec3a0eeae304f139d40bc96a986cf23
msgid "Leisen-Reimer"
msgstr "Leisen-Reimer"

#: ../../maths/american.md:18 f31298e6667d4491873f437294210034
#: f32d7e7f564c4997ad05589ae0d8c138
msgid "derived from the probability"
msgstr "由機率反推而得"

#: ../../maths/american.md:18 f992cdf33f82447c9b5db429ecd20567
msgid "Peizer-Pratt inversion of $d_2$"
msgstr "對 $d_2$ 做 Peizer-Pratt 反轉"

#: ../../maths/american.md:18 4afcb015c2fd47c490a514f5a54b96f9
msgid "Joshi4"
msgstr "Joshi4"

#: ../../maths/american.md:18 7ee9d993a6d84b1aacb5e3e58c958ba7
msgid "a fourth-order variant of the same inversion"
msgstr "同一種反轉的四階變體"

#: ../../maths/american.md:86 4ee0190baaf64478b3e06d8131ffba89
msgid ""
"The classic $u = e^{\\sigma\\sqrt{\\Delta t}},\\ d = 1/u, p = "
"(e^{(r-q)\\Delta t} - d)/(u - d)$ agrees with the Cox-Ross-Rubinstein row"
" to first order in $\\Delta t$; QuantLib's form is the drift-adjusted "
"one."
msgstr "經典的 $u = e^{\\sigma\\sqrt{\\Delta t}},\\ d = 1/u, p = (e^{(r-q)\\Delta t} - d)/(u - d)$ 與 Cox-Ross-Rubinstein 那一列在 $\\Delta t$ 的一階上一致；QuantLib 用的是漂移調整過的形式。"

#: ../../maths/american.md:90 e5a882301f9247be89b53c569460114b
msgid "Which tree to use"
msgstr "該用哪一種樹"

#: ../../maths/american.md:92 1dcf3889c89c47c390320d701c76faaf
msgid ""
"The first five converge to the true price as $O(1/n)$ **with "
"oscillation**: the error changes sign as the strike moves between nodes, "
"so a price plotted against step count zig-zags around the answer. "
"Averaging two adjacent step counts is a cheap way to kill most of that."
msgstr "前五種以 $O(1/n)$ 收斂到真值，但**帶震盪**：當履約價在節點之間移動時誤差會變號，因此把價格對步數畫出來會在答案附近來回鋸齒。取相鄰兩個步數的平均，是消掉其中大部分的便宜做法。"

#: ../../maths/american.md:97 254b3446b62040b5a2453cc614adbb5b
msgid ""
"**Leisen-Reimer** and **Joshi4** are built to remove it. Both invert the "
"binomial probability so that the strike sits exactly between two terminal"
" nodes, both force an **odd** number of steps, and both need the strike —"
" which is why they are strike-aware and the others are not. Their "
"convergence is smooth and roughly $O(1/n^2)$, so a few hundred steps "
"beats a few thousand of the others."
msgstr "**Leisen-Reimer** 與 **Joshi4** 就是為了消除它而設計的。兩者都反推二項機率，使履約價恰好落在兩個期末節點之間；兩者都強制**奇數**步數；兩者都需要履約價——這也是它們會參考履約價而其他樹不會的原因。它們的收斂平滑，約為 $O(1/n^2)$，因此幾百步就勝過其他樹的幾千步。"

#: ../../maths/american.md:104 73b991b86f874c7bb1cfa7ddc9db4750
msgid ""
"For a **barrier** the lattice is Cox-Ross-Rubinstein only, with the "
"Derman-Kani correction that shifts the effective barrier onto the nearest"
" node layer. Barrier lattices converge badly when the barrier falls "
"between nodes, which is exactly what that correction is for; if a barrier"
" price looks unstable in the step count, the finite-difference grid is "
"the better tool."
msgstr "對**障礙**而言，格點僅支援 Cox-Ross-Rubinstein，並帶 Derman-Kani 修正，把有效障礙移到最近的一層節點上。當障礙落在節點之間時，障礙格點收斂得很糟，而那正是這項修正的用途；若某個障礙價格隨步數看起來不穩定，有限差分網格是更好的工具。"

#: ../../maths/american.md:110 03719f57afb248e4b04ee474a4de3b5f
msgid "The alternative: a grid"
msgstr "另一條路：網格"

#: ../../maths/american.md:112 8c070de0b9414329bd51f9e708b1ad71
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Finite difference solves the same free boundary problem by discretising "
"the Black-Scholes equation directly and applying the exercise constraint "
"at every time step. It is the more robust route for a barrier, and the "
"only route this build offers for an American *double* barrier — which it "
"does not have, since the double-barrier engine is analytic and European. "
"See {doc}`numerics`."
msgstr "有限差分直接把 Black-Scholes 方程式離散化，並在每個時間步施加履約條件，藉此求解同一個自由邊界問題。對障礙商品而言它比較穩健，也是這個版本為美式*雙*障礙提供的唯一路徑——而它並不提供，因為雙障礙引擎是解析解且僅限歐式。見 {doc}`numerics`。"

